TSLPRM_USE_MEAS|TSLPRM_USE_MEAS|Optional features||0|1|Record the last measure (0=No, 1=Yes) If No the measure is recalculated using the Reference and Delta
TSLPRM_USE_PROX|TSLPRM_USE_PROX|Optional features||0|1|Proximity detection usage (0=No, 1=Yes)
TSLPRM_USE_ZONE|TSLPRM_USE_ZONE|Optional features||0|1|Zone management usage (0=No, 1=Yes)
TSLPRM_ACQ_MIN|TSLPRM_ACQ_MIN|Acquisition limits||0|65535|Minimum acquisition measurement (range=0..65535) This is the minimum acceptable value for the acquisition measure. The acquisition will be in error IF the measure is below this value.
TSLPRM_ACQ_MAX|TSLPRM_ACQ_MAX|Acquisition limits||0|65535|Maximum acquisition measurement (range=0...65535) This is the maximum acceptable value for the acquisition measure. The acquisition will be in error IF the measure is above this value.
TSLPRM_CALIB_SAMPLES|TSLPRM_CALIB_SAMPLES|Calibration||Max=|Group=|Number of calibration samples (range=4, 8, 16) Low value = faster calibration but less precision. High value = slower calibration but more precision.
TSLPRM_CALIB_DELAY|TSLPRM_CALIB_DELAY|Calibration||0|40|Delay in measurement samples before starting the calibration (range=0..40) - This is useful IF a noise filter is used. - Write 0 to disable the delay.
TSLPRM_TKEY_PROX_IN_TH|TSLPRM_TKEY_PROX_IN_TH|Thresholds for TouchKey sensors||0|255|TouchKeys Proximity state input threshold (range=0..255) Enter Proximity state IF delta is above
TSLPRM_TKEY_PROX_OUT_TH|TSLPRM_TKEY_PROX_OUT_TH|Thresholds for TouchKey sensors||0|255|TouchKeys Proximity state output threshold (range=0..255) Exit Proximity state IF delta is below
TSLPRM_TKEY_DETECT_IN_TH|TSLPRM_TKEY_DETECT_IN_TH|Thresholds for TouchKey sensors||0|255|TouchKeys Detect state input threshold (range=0..255) Enter Detect state IF delta is above
TSLPRM_TKEY_DETECT_OUT_TH|TSLPRM_TKEY_DETECT_OUT_TH|Thresholds for TouchKey sensors||0|255|TouchKeys Detect state output threshold (range=0..255) Exit Detect state IF delta is below
TSLPRM_TKEY_CALIB_TH|TSLPRM_TKEY_CALIB_TH|Thresholds for TouchKey sensors||0|255|TouchKeys re-Calibration threshold (range=0..255) @warning The value is inverted in the sensor state machine Enter Calibration state IF delta is below
TSLPRM_COEFF_TH|TSLPRM_COEFF_TH|Thresholds for TouchKey sensors||0|4|TouchKey, Linear and Rotary sensors thresholds coefficient (range=0..4) This multiplier coefficient is applied on Detect and Re-Calibration thresholds only. 0: feature disabled 1: thresholds x 2 2: thresholds x 4 3: thresholds x 8 4: thresholds x 16
TSLPRM_LINROT_PROX_IN_TH|TSLPRM_LINROT_PROX_IN_TH|Thresholds for Linear and Rotary sensors||0|255|Linear/Rotary Proximity state input threshold (range=0..255) Enter Proximity state IF delta is above
TSLPRM_LINROT_PROX_OUT_TH|TSLPRM_LINROT_PROX_OUT_TH|Thresholds for Linear and Rotary sensors||0|255|Linear/Rotary Proximity state output threshold (range=0..255) Exit Proximity state IF delta is below
TSLPRM_LINROT_DETECT_IN_TH|TSLPRM_LINROT_DETECT_IN_TH|Thresholds for Linear and Rotary sensors||0|255|Linear/Rotary Detect state input threshold (range=0..255) Enter Detect state IF delta is above
TSLPRM_LINROT_DETECT_OUT_TH|TSLPRM_LINROT_DETECT_OUT_TH|Thresholds for Linear and Rotary sensors||0|255|Linear/Rotary Detect state output threshold (range=0..255) Exit Detect state IF delta is below
TSLPRM_LINROT_CALIB_TH|TSLPRM_LINROT_CALIB_TH|Thresholds for Linear and Rotary sensors||0|255|Linear/Rotary re-Calibration threshold (range=0..255) @warning The value is inverted in the sensor state machine Enter Calibration state IF delta is below A low absolute value will result in a higher sensitivity and thus some spurious, recalibration may be issued.
TSLPRM_LINROT_USE_NORMDELTA|TSLPRM_LINROT_USE_NORMDELTA|Thresholds for Linear and Rotary sensors||0|1|Linear/Rotary Delta normalization (0=No, 1=Yes) - When this parameter is set, a coefficient is applied on all Delta of all sensors in order to normalize them and to improve the position calculation. - These coefficients must be defined in a constant table in the application (see Library examples). - The MSB is the coefficient integer part, the LSB is the coefficient real part. - Examples: - To apply a factor 1.10: 0x01 to the MSB 0x1A to the LSB (0.10 x 256 = 25.6 -> rounded to 26 = 0x1A) - To apply a factor 0.90: 0x00 to the MSB 0xE6 to the LSB (0.90 x 256 = 230.4 -> rounded to 230 = 0xE6) - To apply no factor: 0x01 to the MSB 0x00 to the LSB
TSLPRM_LINROT_RESOLUTION|TSLPRM_LINROT_RESOLUTION|Linear/Rotary sensors position||1|8|Position resolution in number of bits (range=1..8) - A Low value will result in a low resolution and will be less subject to noise. - A High value will result in a high resolution and will be more subject to noise.
TSLPRM_LINROT_DIR_CHG_POS|TSLPRM_LINROT_DIR_CHG_POS|Linear/Rotary sensors position||0|255|Direction change threshold in position unit (range=0..255) - Defines the default threshold used during the change direction process. - A Low value will result in a faster direction change. - A High value will result in a slower direction change.
TSLPRM_LINROT_DIR_CHG_DEB|TSLPRM_LINROT_DIR_CHG_DEB|Linear/Rotary sensors position||0|63|Direction change debounce (range=0..63) - Defines the default integrator counter used during the change direction process. - This counter is decremented when the same change in the position is detected and the direction will change after this counter reaches zero. - A Low value will result in a faster direction change. - A High value will result in a slower direction change.
TSLPRM_DEBOUNCE_PROX|TSLPRM_DEBOUNCE_PROX|Debounce counters||0|63|Proximity state debounce in samples unit (range=0..63) - A Low value will result in a higher sensitivity during the Proximity detection but with less noise filtering. - A High value will result in improving the system noise immunity but will increase the system response time.
TSLPRM_DEBOUNCE_DETECT|TSLPRM_DEBOUNCE_DETECT|Debounce counters||0|63|Detect state debounce in samples unit (range=0..63) - A Low value will result in a higher sensitivity during the detection but with less noise filtering. - A High value will result in improving the system noise immunity but will increase the system response time.
TSLPRM_DEBOUNCE_RELEASE|TSLPRM_DEBOUNCE_RELEASE|Debounce counters||0|63|Release state debounce in samples unit (range=0..63) - A Low value will result in a higher sensitivity during the end-detection but with less noise filtering. - A High value will result in a lower sensitivity during the end-detection but with more noise filtering.
TSLPRM_DEBOUNCE_CALIB|TSLPRM_DEBOUNCE_CALIB|Debounce counters||0|63|Re-calibration state debounce in samples unit (range=0..63) - A Low value will result in a higher sensitivity during the recalibration but with less noise filtering. - A High value will result in a lower sensitivity during the recalibration but with more noise filtering.
TSLPRM_DEBOUNCE_ERROR|TSLPRM_DEBOUNCE_ERROR|Debounce counters||0|63|Error state debounce in samples unit (range=0..63) - A Low value will result in a higher sensitivity to enter in error state. - A High value will result in a lower sensitivity to enter in error state.
TSLPRM_ECS_K_SLOW|TSLPRM_ECS_K_SLOW|Environment Change System (ECS)||0|255|Environment Change System Slow K factor (range=0..255) - The higher value is K, the faster is the response time.
TSLPRM_ECS_K_FAST|TSLPRM_ECS_K_FAST|Environment Change System (ECS)||0|255|Environment Change System Fast K factor (range=0..255) - The higher value is K, the faster is the response time.
TSLPRM_ECS_DELAY|TSLPRM_ECS_DELAY|Environment Change System (ECS)||0|5000|Environment Change System delay in msec (range=0..5000) - The ECS will be started after this delay and when all sensors are in Release state.
TSLPRM_DTO|TSLPRM_DTO|Detection Time Out (DTO)||0|63|Detection Time Out delay in seconds (range=0..63) - Value 0: DTO processing not compiled in the code (to gain size IF not used). - Value 1: Default time out infinite. - Value between 2 and 63: Default time out between value n-1 and n. - Examples: - With a DTO equal to 2, the time out is between 1s and 2s. - With a DTO equal to 63, the time out is between 62s and 63s. @note The DTO can be changed in run-time by the application only IF the default value is between 1 and 63.
TSLPRM_USE_DXS|TSLPRM_USE_DXS|Detection Exclusion System (DXS)||0|1|Detection Exclusion System (0=No, 1=Yes)
TSLPRM_TICK_FREQ|TSLPRM_TICK_FREQ|Miscellaneous parameters||||Timing tick frequency in Hz (range=125, 250, 500, 1000, 2000) - Result to a timing interrupt respectively every 8ms, 4ms, 2ms, 1ms, 0.5ms
TSLPRM_DELAY_DISCHARGE_ALL|TSLPRM_DELAY_DISCHARGE_ALL|Miscellaneous parameters||0|65535|Delay for discharging Cx and Cs capacitors (range=0..65535) - The value corresponds to the Softdelay function parameter. - 500 gives around 63 µs delay whatever HCLK - 1000 gives around 125 µs delay whatever HCLK - 2000 gives around 250 µs delay whatever HCLK
TSLPRM_IODEF|TSLPRM_IODEF|Miscellaneous parameters||0|1|IOs default mode when no on-going acquisition (range=0..1) - 0: Output push-pull low - 1: Input floating @note To ensure a correct operation in noisy environment, this parameter should be configured to output push-pull low (excepted for Linear sensors).
TSLPRM_USE_SHIELD|TSLPRM_USE_SHIELD|MCU parameters||0|1|Shield with a channel (0=No, 1=Yes)
TSLPRM_CT_PERIOD|TSLPRM_CT_PERIOD|MCU parameters||0||Charge/transfer Period (in µs) (= high pulse + low pulse) @note For HW acquisition only
TSLPRM_TIMER_FREQ|TSLPRM_TIMER_FREQ|MCU parameters||0||Timer frequency (in MHz) - This is used to calculate the Timer reload value. @note For HW acquisition only
TSLPRM_DELAY_TRANSFER|TSLPRM_DELAY_TRANSFER|MCU parameters||0|65535|Delay for transfering charges from Cx to Cs capacitor and then discharge Cx (range=0..65535) - 0: no delay (it takes about 2.8µs for a CT cycle) - (1..65535): delay (in µs) = 0.75 * TSLPRM_DELAY_TRANSFER + 1 @note for SW acquisition only
TSLPRM_USE_SPREAD_SPECTRUM|TSLPRM_USE_SPREAD_SPECTRUM|MCU parameters||0|1|Use Spread Spectrum (0=No, 1=Yes) @note for SW acquisition only
TSLPRM_SPREAD_MIN|TSLPRM_SPREAD_MIN|MCU parameters||0|=(TSLPRM_SPREAD_MAX-1)|Spread min value (range=0..(TSLPRM_SPREAD_MAX-1)) @note for SW acquisition only
TSLPRM_SPREAD_MAX|TSLPRM_SPREAD_MAX|MCU parameters||2|255|Spread max value (range=2..255) @note for SW acquisition only
TSLPRM_PROTECT_IO_ACCESS|TSLPRM_PROTECT_IO_ACCESS|MCU parameters||0|1|IT disabling for IO protection (range=0..1) - 0: IO not protected - 1: IO protected @note for SW acquisition only
TSLPRM_USE_GPIOA|TSLPRM_USE_GPIOA|MCU parameters||0|1|GPIO to be used (range=0..1) - 0: Not used - 1: Used @note for SW acquisition only
TSLPRM_USE_GPIOB|TSLPRM_USE_GPIOB|MCU parameters||0|1|GPIO to be used (range=0..1) - 0: Not used - 1: Used @note for SW acquisition only
TSLPRM_USE_GPIOC|TSLPRM_USE_GPIOC|MCU parameters||0|1|GPIO to be used (range=0..1) - 0: Not used - 1: Used @note for SW acquisition only
TSLPRM_USE_GPIOF|TSLPRM_USE_GPIOF|MCU parameters||0|1|GPIO to be used (range=0..1) - 0: Not used - 1: Used @note for SW acquisition only
TSLPRM_USE_GPIOG|TSLPRM_USE_GPIOG|MCU parameters||0|1|GPIO to be used (range=0..1) - 0: Not used - 1: Used @note for SW acquisition only
